BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Depth Sewing Intro - Aug 10 [Mondays - 6 week program]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T210000
UID:ttl-11006643273921@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:LEARN TO SEW \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Suitable for beginners. This
  class goes over the basics of operating a sewing machine\, cutting and se
 wing garments\, and basic pattern alterations. \n \n \n The main project f
 or this class is an apron custom fit to YOU. A typical first project is a 
 tote bag\,but we’ve chosen to have our students make an apron as it cove
 rs the same skills while also teaching basic tailoring and fitting. The go
 al of this class is to provide students with the basic skills associated w
 ith sewing\, understanding patterns\, and textiles\, while promoting confi
 dence and shifting the mindset of your everyday clothing as things that su
 it your needs and body\, rather than things to simply wear. \n \n \n \n \n
  \n\n \n \n This class will also explore clothing repairs and minor altera
 tions like hemming\, altering\nnecklines\, adding pockets\, etc. Students 
 are encouraged to bring in items they wish to alter or repair. \n \n \n M
 aterials and equipment for all projects are provided with the course. \n \
 n \n\n \n Schedule \n6 weeks\, Mondays 6pm to 9pm \n \n \n\n \n \n Outcome
 s \n At the end of the course you will have achieved the following goals: 
 \n \n \n- Proficiency with operating a sewing machine safely \n\n- Underst
 anding of fabric types\, their uses\, how to prep them for sewing\, and ho
 w to cut fabric \n\n- Comfort with taking measurements of the body and how
  to apply them to a pattern \n\n- Knowledge of basic pattern alterations a
 nd how to adjust existing garments to fit you better \n\n- Understanding o
 f how to transfer patterns to fabric so that space is used as efficiently 
 as possible \n\n- Understanding of pinning and ironing techniques \n\n- Fa
 miliarity with basic sewing techniques including seams\, hemming\, hand st
 itching\,\napplying pockets\, fasteners including buttons\, zippers\, snap
 s\, and ties\, as well as\ndifferent stitch uses for different techniques 
 and materials\n\n- Basic repairs like fixing holes\, torn seams\, holes in
  pockets\, adding patches\n\n- Basic alterations like adjusting hems\, cha
 nging necklines\, switching out buttons or other fasteners
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/in-depth-sewing-intro-aug-3-mondays-6-w
 eek-program
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In-Depth Intro to Woodworking Aug 9 [Sundays - 6 week Intensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260809T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260809T130000
UID:ttl-11006631641281@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Description: \n\n \n Suitable for beginners\, this woodworkin
 g course is designed to teach you all that you need to get started in wood
 working by learning both traditional\, and modern techniques.\n\n Students
  will learn valuable hands-on skills working on instructor-lead projects u
 sing both hand and power tools.\n\n Projects are chosen to provide skills 
 development in a natural progression from familiarity with the unique char
 acteristics of wood\, to basic essential techniques\, to some more advance
 d topics.\n\n Materials and equipment for all projects are provided with t
 he course.\n\n \n\n Schedule : \n\n Six three-hour weekly classes\, Sunda
 ys 10am to 1pm. \n\n Outcomes : \n\n At the end of this course you will ha
 ve achieved the following goals: \n\n \n- A complete understanding of the 
 nature and properties of wood \n\n- Proficiency with traditional woodworki
 ng techniques\n\n- Comfort working with chisels\, planes\, saws\n\n- Profi
 ciency with wood milling techniques\n\n- Comfort with safe operation of p
 ower tools\n\n- Familiarity with power planing\, joiner\, drill press\, ro
 uter and table saw \n\n- Dressing and laminating wood \n\n- Experience fo
 llowing project plans \n\n- Familiarity with joinery \n\n- Wood finishing\
 , various treatments \n\n \n  Following this course\, you'll be certified
  to use the woodshop. And you'll be able to join the growing community of 
 TTL Makers sharing knowledge on our Discord community.\n\n Certifications 
 for all courses are valid for one year from the time that they are issued\
 , and can be renewed at no cost with your active monthly membership within
  3 months of their expiry. Certification renewal requires booking with an 
 instructor\, is conducted at the makerspace\, and helps you keep your skil
 ls current. \n\nUseful for: furniture\, cabinets\, organisers\, cutting-b
 oards \n \n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes are posted? \n\n 
 Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/in-depth-intro-to-woodworking-aug-9-sun
 days-6-week-intensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Battlebots Summer Camp Aug 17-21 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T160000
UID:ttl-10932875100353@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Battlebots Camp \n\n \n \n Recommended Ages 8-13 \n \n \n\n \n
  \n \n \n\n \n \n For a whole week we will work in teams to design and bui
 ld a working remote controlled robot. We will add various kinetic weapons.
  The end of the week will feature epic battles that parents might not want
  to miss.\n\n We will learn the basics of electronics and robotics using s
 oldering Irons\, laser cuttters and 3d printers\n\n \n \n \n Note: Battleb
 ots will be disassembled following the camp\, for use in our ongoing weekl
 y programs. TTL teaches kids to reduce\, re-use\, and recycle parts into n
 ew projects!\n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Day 1 - Monday \n \n \n \n \n \n T
 ransmitters and Receivers. Electronic Basics\, Soldering\n\n We will spend
  the day learning the basics of electrical circuits\, motors and eventural
 ly learning to operate the remote control boards. The afternoon will cover
  gears\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Day 2 - Tuesday \n \n \n \n \n \n Robots a
 nd Cad design. 3D printind and Laser cutting.\n\n We will begin the mornin
 g with a lesson on the use of 3d printers\, the software used to create 3d
  objects as well as the program used to slice the 3d object into layers.\n
 \n The afternoon will have kids learning 2d modeling and use of laser cutt
 ers and engravers.\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Day 3 - Wednesday \n \n \n \n 
 \n \n Design and Build – Electronics\, 3d printing\, laser cutting and C
 AD Design\n\n The kids will be separated into 2 groups and will start to d
 esign and plan the building of remote controlled robots. By the end of the
  day the robot should either be able to move or only require 3d prints to 
 be completed to do so.\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Day 4 - Thursday \n \n \n 
 \n \n \n Attack and Defence – Design\, 3d printing\, Laser cutting and E
 lectronics\n\n Additional design features will be added to allow the robot
 s to compete against one another in a specific arena. A strategy for compe
 tition should be under way. Kids will have all day to experiment and build
 .\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Day 5  - Friday \n \n \n \n \n \n \n T
 he kids will have the morning to finish and decorate the robots\, Create t
 he arena\, Add features to it\n\n The afternoon kids will practice control
 ling the robot and completing a number of challenges.\n\n At 3:30 We will 
 begin our main event and the robots will be pitted against each other in a
  battle\n\n to the finish. Parents will not want to miss it\, but maybe br
 ing ear protection. It gets LOUD.\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n About Kids Camp
 s at TTLMakerspace \n \n \n We love our young makers at TTLMakerspace\, an
 d run kids programs all year long for our active members. Our summer camps
  provide the opportunity for curious young builders to have a very hands-o
 n experience mastering tools both traditional and high-tech. \n \n \n\n \n
  Schedule \n \n \n \n\n \n Drop off 8:45 to 9:00 am \n \n \n 9:15  am  s
 kill training \n \n \n 10:30 am  Break and Snacks \n \n \n 10:45 am  Bui
 lding Session 1 \n \n \n 12:00 pm  Lunch (At the Grange Park weather perm
 itting) Kids will be required to bring a lunch and we recommend a re-usabl
 e water bottle that they can refill during the week. \n \n \n 1:00  pm  
 Building Session 2 \n \n \n 2:30  pm  Break and Snacks \n \n \n 2:45  p
 m  Building Session 3 \n \n \n 3:45  pm Cleaning \n \n \n Pick up 4:00 t
 o 4:15 pm with extended care available for an additional fee.
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/battlebots-summer-camp-aug-17-21-2026
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DangerCamp Summer Camp Aug 10-14 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T160000
UID:ttl-10932862255297@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:The Science of FUN \n\n \n \n Recommended Ages 8-11 \n \n \n\n
  \n While we prioritise safety - we want to empower kids! We equip youths 
 with the knowledge and guidance needed to safely create in a community mak
 erspace environment. With close supervision\, kids will use various tools 
 and technology including Laser Cutters\, 3d Printers\, and Electronics. \n
  \n \n\n \n \n Day 1 - Monday \n Plasma Cannons -  science skills \n \n \
 n The group will learn about blast effects\, energy release and material b
 ehaviour while working as a group to create working plasma cannons. These 
 will create an incredible pyrotechnic display while being completely harml
 ess. These will be dismantled at the end of the day. \n \n \n Day 2 - Tues
 day \n Bottle Rockets and a Launcher  - design and tool use \n \n \n Buil
 ding a bottle rocket offers a hands-on\, engaging way to explore fundament
 al physics concepts and provides a fun and educational activity. It's a gr
 eat way to see how forces\, like the release of compressed air or water\, 
 can propel an object into the air.\nThe rockets spray water everywhere so 
 we may need to move this activity to a day with accommodating weather. We 
 will go to the park at lunch to launch our rockets.\n\n \n \n \n Day 3 - W
 ednesday \n Spy Telescope - science\, STEM\, tool use \n \n \n Building a 
 telescope provides hands-on experience with optics\, STEM concepts\, and t
 he principles of how telescopes work. Students will experiment with differ
 ent lenses then design and create a telescope  \n \n \n Day 4 - Thursday 
 \n Sleeve Water Pistols and Decoder Wheels. \n \n \n The morning will be s
 pent designing and building quick deploying fire suppression (water) pisto
 ls that strap to your wrist for efficiency. These will be tested at the pa
 rk during lunch. The afternoon will have the kids create their own secret 
 encryption device.\n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n Day 5  - Friday \n \n Remote Cont
 rolled Bomb Disarming Robot - robotics \n \n \n The kids will have all day
  to design and build a robot that will allow them to disable a special sur
 prise. They will rely on the skills they have accumulated over the week to
  problem solve as a group.  \n \n \n\n \n About Kids Camps at TTLMakerspa
 ce \n \n \n We love our young makers at TTLMakerspace\, and run kids progr
 ams all year long for our active members. Our summer camps provide the opp
 ortunity for curious young builders to have a very hands-on experience mas
 tering tools both traditional and high-tech. \n \n \n\n \n Schedule \n \n 
 \n \n\n \n Drop off 8:45 to 9:00 am \n \n \n 9:15  am  skill training \n
  \n \n 10:30 am  Break and Snacks \n \n \n 10:45 am  Building Session 1 
 \n \n \n 12:00 pm  Lunch (At the Grange Park weather permitting) Kids wil
 l be required to bring a lunch and we recommend a re-usable water bottle t
 hat they can refill during the week. \n \n \n 1:00  pm  Building Session
  2 \n \n \n 2:30  pm  Break and Snacks \n \n \n 2:45  pm  Building Ses
 sion 3 \n \n \n 3:45  pm Cleaning \n \n \n Pick up 4:00 to 4:15 pm with e
 xtended care available for an additional fee.
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/dangercamp-summer-camp-aug-10-14-2027
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
